1
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:00,800
<i>The war had all but ground to a halt
in the blink of an eye.</i>

2
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:07,500
<i>Lucian, the most feared and ruthless
leader ever to rule the lycan clan...</i>

3
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:10,300
<i>...had finally been killed.</i>

4
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,700
<i>The lycan horde
scattered to the wind...</i>

5
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,500
<i>...in a single evening
of flame and retribution.</i>

6
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,900
<i>Victory, it seemed, was in our grasp...</i>

7
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,900
<i>...the very birthright of the vampires.</i>

8
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,100
<i>Nearly six centuries had passed
since that night.</i>

9
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,700
<i>Yet the ancient feud proved unwilling
to follow Lucian to the grave.</i>

10
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:44,800
<i>Though lycans were
fewer in number...</i>

11
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,300
<i>...the war itself had become
more perilous.</i>

12
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,500
<i>For the moon no longer
held her sway.</i>

13
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,200
<i>Older, more powerful lycans
were now able to change at will.</i>

14
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,700
<i>The weapons had evolved,
but our orders remained the same:</i>

15
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,800
<i>Hunt them down and kill them off,
one by one.</i>

16
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:09,100
<i>A most successful campaign.</i>

17
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:12,000
<i>Perhaps too successful.</i>

18
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:25,200
<i>For those like me, a death dealer...</i>

19
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,200
<i>...this signaled the end of an era.</i>

20
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,900
<i>Like the weapons
of the previous century...</i>

21
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:34,300
<i>...we, too, would become obsolete.</i>

22
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:37,200
<i>Pity, because I lived for it.</i>

23
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:24,000
Bloods!

24
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:50,200
It's all right. It's all right.
You're gonna be okay.

25
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,800
You're acting like a pack
of rabid dogs!

26
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,600
And that, gentlemen...

27
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,500
...simply will not do.

28
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:34,900
Not if you expect to defeat
the vampires on their own ground.

29
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:39,300
Not if you expect to survive at all.

30
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:42,300
Pierce! Taylor!

31
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,300
Put some clothes on, will you?

32
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:28,600
We have a serious problem.

33
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:45,800
I'll have to run a few tests.

34
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:48,900
It's definitely an irradiated fluid
of some sort.

35
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:50,700
Ultraviolet ammunition.

36
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,800
Daylight, harnessed as a weapon.

37
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:56,100
You expect me to believe
that a mangy animal...

38
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:59,600
...came up with a bullet specifically
engineered to kill vampires?

39
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:01,400
No, I'm betting it's military.

40
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:04,600
Something they stole.
Some sort of high-tech tracer round.

41
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:07,100
I don't care where
they got these things.

42
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:10,000
Rigel is dead, and Nathaniel
could still be out there.

43
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,600
Let's gather the death dealers
and go back.

44
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:15,600
Absolutely not. Not now.
Not for a random incursion.

45
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:20,100
The awakening is a few days off,
and this house is in unrest as it is.

46
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:23,700
Random? They opened fire on us
in full view of the public.

47
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:28,200
- And from what I heard in that tunnel...
- you said you didn't see anything.

48
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:32,100
I know what I heard,
and I know what my gut tells me.

49
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:34,500
There could be dozens
of lycans down there.

50
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,600
Who knows, maybe more. Hundreds.

51
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:39,700
We've hunted them
to the brink of extinction.

52
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:42,800
Kraven's right, Selene.

53
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:46,100
There's not been a den
of that magnitude for centuries.

54
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:49,300
- Not since the days of Lucian.
- I know that, Kahn.

55
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:51,900
But I'd rather you prove me wrong
by checking it out.

56
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,500
Have your men tighten things up.

57
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:57,800
I'll have Soren assemble
a search team.

58
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:03,500
- No, I want to lead the team myself.
- Absolutely not! Soren will handle it.

59
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:06,400
Hundreds, really?

60
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,500
Viktor would believe me.

61
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:16,400
- I'd never treat you like that.
- Of course not.

62
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:21,700
Now run along and make sure she's
dressed and ready for her guests.

63
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:34,200
- It's a waste of time, you know.
- What is?

64
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:38,300
I doubt Viktor would want you freezing
in here, staring at his tomb for hours.

65
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:43,400
No, he'd want the death dealers out
there, scouring every inch of the city.

66
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:48,100
Kraven. I'll never understand
why Viktor left him in charge.

67
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:50,700
He's a bureaucrat, not a warrior.

68
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:53,100
We need to get you ready.

69
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,500
- For what?
- The party.

70
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,400
Amelia's envoy will be here
any minute.

71
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:58,100
Oh, yes.

72
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:01,300
You should definitely wear this one.
It's perfect.

73
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,700
They were after you.

74
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:38,300
He's attractive...

75
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:40,800
...for a human.
- Who's attractive?

76
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:57,300
I planned to have you
at my side this evening.

77
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,800
Take Erika.
She's dying to be at your side.

78
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:07,000
If you ask me, you take this warrior
business far too seriously.

79
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:12,700
You can't undo the past,
no matter how many you kill.

80
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:15,300
And besides...

81
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:17,500
...what's the point
in being immortal...

82
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:20,400
...if you deny yourself
life's simple pleasures?

83
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,400
Do you see this human?

84
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:26,500
- What of him?
- I'm beginning to think the lycans...

85
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:28,000
Blast!

86
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:35,900
Put on something elegant
and be quick about it.

87
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,400
Kraven, I'm serious.
I think they were following him.

88
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,300
Other than food,
why would lycans stalk a human?

89
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:00,700
Any progress?

90
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:03,200
Let's find out.

91
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:12,900
Negative.

92
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:30,400
You heading home?

93
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:33,900
Yeah, Nicholas gave me
a couple hours off.

94
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,900
By the way...

95
00:20:36,300 --> 00:20:39,500
...he said you did a terrific job
tonight with the surgery.

96
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,200
Yeah.

97
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:45,900
Take it easy.

98
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:43,500
We were ambushed.

99
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:45,300
Death dealers, three of them.

100
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:48,100
- And the candidate?
- We lost him.

101
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:49,100
You lost him?

102
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:53,100
Look at this mess.

103
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:56,300
Ag rounds. High content.

104
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:58,600
Prevented him from
making the change.

105
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:07,100
No use in digging out the rest.
Silver's penetrated his organs.

106
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:10,100
Regeneration's impossible
at this point.

107
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,600
Let's take these out.

108
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,700
Relax.

109
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:30,700
The vampires didn't realize
you were following a human...

110
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:34,000
...did they, raze?
- No.

111
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:37,600
I mean, I don't think so.

112
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:41,500
- You don't think, or you don't know?
- I'm not sure.

113
00:22:59,100 --> 00:23:00,800
Negative.

114
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:04,800
I really must have a look
at this Michael.

115
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:08,300
Must I do everything myself?

116
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:25,500
Our noble houses may be
separated by a great ocean...

117
00:23:25,500 --> 00:23:30,500
...but we are equally committed
to the survival of the bloodlines.

118
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:33,500
And when Amelia arrives
to awaken Marcus...

119
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:37,100
...in just two days' time...

120
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:42,000
...we shall once again
be united as a single coven!

121
00:23:45,500 --> 00:23:50,200
We want to thank our hosts
for their generous hospitality.

122
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:55,400
<i>He comes in, he does his job
and then he goes home.</i>

123
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:58,500
<i>Other than that,
I don't know what to tell you.</i>

124
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:02,000
<i>Interns work around the clock.
We don't have much of a life.</i>

125
00:25:02,300 --> 00:25:04,600
You know where we can find him?

126
00:25:04,900 --> 00:25:06,200
No.

127
00:25:06,900 --> 00:25:10,900
You can try him at home,
or you'll have to wait till he gets back.

128
00:25:12,900 --> 00:25:15,100
He's not in some kind
of trouble, is he?

129
00:26:00,700 --> 00:26:04,400
<i>This is Michael. I'm not in right now.
Please leave a message.</i>

130
00:26:04,700 --> 00:26:08,500
<i>Michael, it's Adam. The police were
just in the hospital looking for you.</i>

131
00:26:08,700 --> 00:26:11,600
<i>They were convinced you were
involved with a shootout.</i>

132
00:26:11,700 --> 00:26:14,700
<i>I told them there's no way
you'd be involved with that...</i>

133
00:26:14,700 --> 00:26:16,900
<i>...but they're looking for you.
Right now.</i>

134
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:23,000
Why are they after you?

135
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:48,700
Shit!

136
00:27:35,300 --> 00:27:36,600
Hello, Michael.

137
00:29:04,700 --> 00:29:06,200
What the fuck is going on?

138
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:52,600
Stop the car.

139
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:55,900
Stop the car!

140
00:30:56,300 --> 00:30:57,800
Back off!

141
00:30:57,800 --> 00:30:59,200
Okay.

142
00:31:00,100 --> 00:31:01,500
Okay.

143
00:31:03,100 --> 00:31:04,500
All right.

144
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:10,300
But you've lost a lot of blood.

145
00:31:10,600 --> 00:31:13,400
If you don't stop the car,
you'll get us both killed.

146
00:31:15,500 --> 00:31:18,300
- I'm not screwing around!
- Neither am I!

147
00:31:18,500 --> 00:31:20,300
Shut up and hold on.
I'll be fine.

148
00:31:25,900 --> 00:31:27,000
Shit!

149
00:33:08,300 --> 00:33:11,200
A second escape. Impressive.

150
00:33:11,800 --> 00:33:13,800
Perhaps raze wasn't
overstating matters.

151
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:16,400
Raze didn't bring back this.

152
00:33:28,300 --> 00:33:32,000
If Michael is indeed the carrier,
the vampires could...

153
00:33:32,300 --> 00:33:34,900
relax, old friend.

154
00:33:35,300 --> 00:33:37,000
I've tasted his flesh.

155
00:33:37,800 --> 00:33:39,900
Just two days till full moon.

156
00:33:41,300 --> 00:33:43,900
Soon, he will be a lycan.

157
00:33:44,300 --> 00:33:47,400
Soon, he will come looking for us.

158
00:34:07,800 --> 00:34:10,900
It's a shame we don't have more.

159
00:34:25,300 --> 00:34:27,500
Positive.

160
00:35:13,300 --> 00:35:16,600
Lay still. Your skull's
taken a good knock.

161
00:35:17,300 --> 00:35:19,700
You've been unconscious
for a while.

162
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:24,500
Do you have any idea
why those men were after you?

163
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:26,500
Where am I?

164
00:35:27,300 --> 00:35:29,000
You're safe.

165
00:35:33,300 --> 00:35:35,200
I'm Selene.

166
00:35:47,300 --> 00:35:50,300
So, for once, the rumors were true.

167
00:35:53,300 --> 00:35:58,000
The whole house has been absolutely
buzzing about your new pet.

168
00:36:00,300 --> 00:36:05,100
- Are you going to try to turn him?
- Of course not.

169
00:36:05,300 --> 00:36:08,000
So why did you bring him here?

170
00:36:10,300 --> 00:36:11,700
He saved my life.

171
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:17,000
- Why are you here?
- Kraven sent me.

172
00:36:17,300 --> 00:36:20,100
He wants to see you. Now.

173
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:25,200
This is completely unacceptable!

174
00:36:26,800 --> 00:36:30,400
You go against my orders and spend
the night away from the mansion...

175
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:34,300
...with a human? A human you've
since brought back to my house.

176
00:36:34,300 --> 00:36:38,500
As far as I'm concerned,
this is still Viktor's house.

177
00:36:40,300 --> 00:36:42,200
Look, I don't want to argue.

178
00:36:42,300 --> 00:36:45,400
Understand that Michael is somehow
important to the lycans...

179
00:36:45,500 --> 00:36:48,400
- so now it's "Michael"!
- Would you just hear me out?

180
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:52,400
It's beyond me why you're so
obsessed over this ridiculous theory.

181
00:36:52,400 --> 00:36:54,800
Lucian wouldn't be a bit
interested in a human...

182
00:36:55,300 --> 00:36:57,900
...Michael or otherwise.

183
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:02,100
Wait a minute.

184
00:37:03,800 --> 00:37:05,900
You're infatuated with him,
aren't you?

185
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:08,000
Now, that's a ridiculous theory.

186
00:37:08,600 --> 00:37:09,900
Is it?

187
00:38:34,200 --> 00:38:36,400
Leave us!

188
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:13,000
I sure hope you never get
pissed off with me.

189
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:15,100
Hold on.

190
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:18,600
Check this out.

191
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:26,300
Go ahead. Squeeze off a few.

192
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:41,200
Eject the mag.

193
00:39:44,500 --> 00:39:48,300
You've copied the lycan rounds.
Silver nitrate.

194
00:39:48,300 --> 00:39:49,700
A lethal dose.

195
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:52,500
They won't dig these out,
like our usual rounds.

196
00:39:52,500 --> 00:39:56,000
Straight into the bloodstream.
Ain't nothing to dig out.

197
00:40:00,300 --> 00:40:02,300
Tell me, Kahn.

198
00:40:02,800 --> 00:40:05,300
Do you believe Lucian died
the way they say?

199
00:40:05,300 --> 00:40:08,600
- Kraven telling war stories again?
- That's my point.

200
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:12,000
It's nothing but an ancient story.
His story.

201
00:40:12,300 --> 00:40:15,500
There's not a shred of proof
he killed Lucian, only his word.

202
00:40:15,800 --> 00:40:18,700
I've never underestimated
Kraven's lust for advancement...

203
00:40:18,800 --> 00:40:21,700
...but Viktor believed him
and that's all that matters.

204
00:40:21,800 --> 00:40:24,700
- Where you going with this anyway?
- Nowhere.

205
00:40:46,500 --> 00:40:49,900
Engaging death dealers in public
and chasing after some human...

206
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:54,200
...was not what I had in mind. You
were told to set up shop and lay low!

207
00:40:54,500 --> 00:40:57,600
Calm yourself, Kraven!

208
00:40:59,500 --> 00:41:03,300
The human doesn't concern you.

209
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:09,200
And besides, I've laid low
for quite long enough.

210
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:22,500
Just keep your men at bay, Lucian.

211
00:41:22,500 --> 00:41:24,400
At least for the time being.

212
00:41:24,500 --> 00:41:28,800
Don't force me to regret
our arrangement.

213
00:41:29,100 --> 00:41:31,600
You just concentrate on your part.

214
00:41:32,100 --> 00:41:36,300
Remember, I've bled for you
once already.

215
00:41:36,600 --> 00:41:39,200
Without me, you'd have nothing.

216
00:41:39,200 --> 00:41:42,400
You'd be nothing.

217
00:43:27,900 --> 00:43:31,300
<i>Of the scores of brave souls
who entered Lucian's fortress...</i>

218
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:35,400
<i>...a single vampire survived:
Kraven...</i>

219
00:43:35,400 --> 00:43:39,200
<i>...who was richly rewarded
for not only setting the great blaze...</i>

220
00:43:39,600 --> 00:43:43,600
<i>...but for returning with evidence
of the lycan master's demise...</i>

221
00:43:43,700 --> 00:43:47,700
<i>...the branded skin,
cut from Lucian's very arm.</i>

222
00:44:16,300 --> 00:44:19,100
I've been looking for you.
He's been bitten.

223
00:44:20,800 --> 00:44:23,200
Your human,
he's been marked by a lycan.

224
00:44:25,800 --> 00:44:27,700
- Did Kraven put you up to this?
- No.

225
00:44:27,800 --> 00:44:31,300
I saw the wound with my own eyes,
I swear it.

226
00:44:33,800 --> 00:44:36,000
But what about the covenant?

227
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:38,100
You know it's forbidden!

228
00:44:45,900 --> 00:44:48,700
And ever since he bit me,
I've been...

229
00:44:49,900 --> 00:44:54,300
I've been having these hallucinations
and these delusions.

230
00:44:56,400 --> 00:45:00,700
All I know is, it feels like
my skull is splitting in half.

231
00:45:00,900 --> 00:45:03,400
Okay, so a full-grown man bit you?

232
00:45:05,900 --> 00:45:07,900
Jesus.

233
00:45:08,400 --> 00:45:10,200
Are you sure this wasn't a dog?

234
00:45:10,200 --> 00:45:12,600
I said, it was a man.
It was a man.

235
00:45:12,700 --> 00:45:16,000
- Okay, I got it.
- He was after me.

236
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:19,800
- And that woman from the subway...
- what woman?

237
00:45:20,700 --> 00:45:24,000
Haven't you been listening to me?
She took me hostage!

238
00:45:24,200 --> 00:45:25,700
All right.

239
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:27,400
Just... please.

240
00:45:28,500 --> 00:45:32,300
I'll help you get this all sorted out,
all right? I'll be right back.

241
00:45:34,500 --> 00:45:36,500
Let go, Michael.

242
00:45:37,100 --> 00:45:38,600
Let go.

243
00:45:39,100 --> 00:45:43,200
Just calm down, okay?
I'm gonna be back in a minute.

244
00:45:43,600 --> 00:45:46,500
- That's a promise.
- All right.

245
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:57,200
Please forgive me...

246
00:46:57,500 --> 00:47:00,400
...but I desperately need
your guidance.

247
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:08,200
Kahn wants to see you.

248
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:49,300
<i>To my knowledge...</i>

249
00:48:49,500 --> 00:48:54,000
<i>...an awakening has never been
attempted by one such as myself.</i>

250
00:48:54,500 --> 00:48:58,000
<i>The elders hold the power to organize
their memories and thoughts...</i>

251
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:00,200
<i>...into a single, cohesive vision...</i>

252
00:49:00,500 --> 00:49:03,500
<i>...a detailed record of their reign.</i>

253
00:49:03,500 --> 00:49:07,400
<i>I can only hope Viktor
will hear my plea.</i>

254
00:50:16,800 --> 00:50:20,400
Please forgive me,
but I desperately need your guidance.

255
00:50:21,500 --> 00:50:24,600
I apologize for awakening you
ahead of schedule...

256
00:50:24,600 --> 00:50:27,100
...but I fear we may all be
in grave danger.

257
00:50:28,500 --> 00:50:32,100
Especially you, my lord,
if left in your weakened state.

258
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:35,700
For I believe that Lucian
is alive and well.

259
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:40,200
Here. Now. In this very city...

260
00:50:40,300 --> 00:50:43,500
...preparing to hit us
during the awakening ceremony.

261
00:50:44,800 --> 00:50:46,900
Even more disturbing...

262
00:50:48,200 --> 00:50:50,100
...is that if I'm correct...

263
00:50:51,200 --> 00:50:53,900
...it would mean that Kraven
is in league with him.

264
00:52:16,400 --> 00:52:18,400
What's so pressing?

265
00:52:18,900 --> 00:52:20,800
Take a look.

266
00:52:39,900 --> 00:52:41,600
Selene!

267
00:52:41,900 --> 00:52:43,900
<i>I want to speak with Selene!</i>

268
00:52:47,700 --> 00:52:49,500
Is that Michael?

269
00:52:49,700 --> 00:52:52,600
- Is it Michael?
- What the hell is going on?

270
00:52:52,700 --> 00:52:54,000
<i>What's happening to me?</i>

271
00:52:56,200 --> 00:52:57,200
<i>I'm coming out.</i>

272
00:52:58,700 --> 00:53:02,300
If you go to him, you'll never
be welcome in this house again.

273
00:53:05,700 --> 00:53:09,100
Now that Viktor's awake, we'll see
what he has to say about that.

274
00:53:22,500 --> 00:53:23,500
Get in.

275
00:53:49,500 --> 00:53:52,600
Look, I warned her. I warned her,
but she didn't listen.

276
00:53:52,600 --> 00:53:55,800
- I should've told you sooner.
- Told me what?

277
00:53:58,600 --> 00:54:00,900
Her human, Michael...

278
00:54:02,100 --> 00:54:04,500
...he's not a human at all.

279
00:54:04,600 --> 00:54:05,700
He's a lycan.

280
00:54:09,600 --> 00:54:11,000
What?

281
00:54:11,100 --> 00:54:14,700
What's this ruckus?

282
00:54:18,600 --> 00:54:21,100
Never come here again.
They'll kill you.

283
00:54:21,500 --> 00:54:24,500
Why? Who are you people?

284
00:55:08,800 --> 00:55:09,800
Leave us.

285
00:55:18,300 --> 00:55:23,000
Like it or not, you're in the middle
of a war that's raged for 1000 years.

286
00:55:23,300 --> 00:55:26,400
A blood feud between
vampires and lycans.

287
00:55:27,800 --> 00:55:28,900
Werewolves.

288
00:55:42,100 --> 00:55:43,400
Consider yourself lucky.

289
00:55:43,600 --> 00:55:46,800
Most humans die within an hour
of being bitten by an immortal.

290
00:55:47,100 --> 00:55:49,000
The viruses we transmit are deadly.

291
00:55:49,100 --> 00:55:52,300
And if you bit me,
I'd become a vampire instead?

292
00:55:52,600 --> 00:55:53,900
No, you'd die.

293
00:55:54,600 --> 00:55:57,900
No one's ever survived
a bite from both species.

294
00:55:58,100 --> 00:56:00,600
By rights, I'd stop the car
and kill you myself...

295
00:56:01,100 --> 00:56:03,000
- why are you helping me?
- I'm not.

296
00:56:03,100 --> 00:56:05,600
I track down and kill your kind.

297
00:56:05,600 --> 00:56:09,200
My only interest is finding out
why Lucian wants you so badly.

298
00:56:12,800 --> 00:56:15,800
Do you know why I've
been awakened, servant?

299
00:56:15,800 --> 00:56:17,600
No, my lord.

300
00:56:17,800 --> 00:56:21,200
- But I'll soon find out.
- You mean when you find her.

301
00:56:21,800 --> 00:56:25,300
- Yes, my lord.
- You must let her come to me.

302
00:56:26,300 --> 00:56:30,800
We have much to discuss,
Selene and I.

303
00:56:31,800 --> 00:56:37,200
She has shown me
a great many disturbing things.

304
00:56:37,300 --> 00:56:40,600
Things that will be dealt with
soon enough.

305
00:56:40,800 --> 00:56:44,700
This coven has grown weak,
decadent.

306
00:56:44,800 --> 00:56:50,100
Perhaps I should have left someone
else in charge of my affairs.

307
00:56:54,800 --> 00:56:56,700
Still...

308
00:56:57,300 --> 00:56:59,600
...her memories...

309
00:57:00,300 --> 00:57:02,800
...are chaotic.

310
00:57:04,300 --> 00:57:05,800
There's no sense of time.

311
00:57:05,800 --> 00:57:08,200
Please, my lord,
let me summon assistance.

312
00:57:08,300 --> 00:57:10,000
You're in need of rest.

313
00:57:10,800 --> 00:57:14,000
I've rested enough.

314
00:57:14,800 --> 00:57:17,800
What you will do
is summon Marcus.

315
00:57:21,200 --> 00:57:24,600
But he still slumbers, my lord.

316
00:57:26,200 --> 00:57:29,900
Amelia and the council members
are arriving tomorrow night...

317
00:57:30,200 --> 00:57:32,200
...to awaken Marcus.

318
00:57:32,700 --> 00:57:34,600
Not you, my lord.

319
00:57:34,700 --> 00:57:38,800
You've been awakened
a full century ahead of schedule.

320
00:57:47,600 --> 00:57:49,900
That bitch has betrayed me.

321
00:57:50,600 --> 00:57:54,400
Now he knows everything
she's been obsessing about.

322
00:57:58,200 --> 00:57:59,900
Wait.

323
00:58:05,200 --> 00:58:07,000
Are you to be trusted?

324
00:58:07,700 --> 00:58:09,600
Of course.

325
00:58:10,200 --> 00:58:12,200
Meet me in my quarters
in 20 minutes.

326
00:58:12,700 --> 00:58:15,700
It's time I filled you in
on a few things.

327
00:58:55,400 --> 00:58:59,300
I'm seeing these things,
these hallucinations.

328
00:58:59,900 --> 00:59:02,400
They're not hallucinations,
they're memories.

329
00:59:02,400 --> 00:59:06,200
You've been bitten. His memories
have been passed to you.

330
00:59:09,100 --> 00:59:14,500
This is one of the places we use
for interrogations. It should be safe.

331
00:59:29,700 --> 00:59:32,600
- Ziodex industries.
- We own it.

332
00:59:32,700 --> 00:59:35,500
First there was synthetic plasma,
now this.

333
00:59:35,700 --> 00:59:38,500
Once it's approved,
it should be our newest cash crop.

334
00:59:38,700 --> 00:59:40,600
It's cloned blood.

335
00:59:46,500 --> 00:59:47,700
What are these for?

336
00:59:50,000 --> 00:59:52,000
Lycans are allergic to silver.

337
00:59:52,000 --> 00:59:55,600
If we don't get our bullets out quickly,
they die during questioning.

338
00:59:56,400 --> 00:59:58,100
What do you do with them after?

339
00:59:59,900 --> 01:00:01,800
We put the bullets back in.

340
01:00:17,500 --> 01:00:20,400
- How are things progressing?
- We're ready.

341
01:00:26,600 --> 01:00:29,200
Why do you hate them so much?

342
01:00:29,600 --> 01:00:32,300
I've already told you,
we're at war.

343
01:00:32,600 --> 01:00:34,400
So you're just following orders?

344
01:00:42,600 --> 01:00:45,700
Why can't you just answer
the question?

345
01:00:48,400 --> 01:00:49,900
Fine.

346
01:00:51,400 --> 01:00:53,800
Something was in the stable...

347
01:00:53,900 --> 01:00:56,900
...tearing our horses to pieces.

348
01:00:58,400 --> 01:01:00,900
I couldn't have saved my mother.

349
01:01:01,000 --> 01:01:03,300
Or my sister.

350
01:01:03,900 --> 01:01:06,600
Their screams woke me.

351
01:01:06,900 --> 01:01:11,200
My father died outside,
trying to fend them off.

352
01:01:11,800 --> 01:01:14,300
I stood at my door...

353
01:01:15,300 --> 01:01:18,800
...about to run
to my nieces' room when...

354
01:01:24,800 --> 01:01:27,100
twin girls.

355
01:01:29,300 --> 01:01:31,800
Barely 6 years old.

356
01:01:33,300 --> 01:01:34,800
Butchered...

357
01:01:35,300 --> 01:01:38,300
...like animals.
- Jesus christ.

358
01:01:38,300 --> 01:01:41,300
The next thing I knew,
I was in his arms.

359
01:01:41,800 --> 01:01:44,800
The war had spilled into our house.

360
01:01:44,800 --> 01:01:47,700
He'd been tracking the lycans
for days.

361
01:01:48,300 --> 01:01:50,500
He drove them off and saved me.

362
01:01:50,600 --> 01:01:53,000
- Who?
- Viktor.

363
01:01:54,300 --> 01:01:57,200
The oldest and strongest of us.

364
01:01:57,800 --> 01:02:00,800
That night,
he made me a vampire.

365
01:02:01,300 --> 01:02:04,300
He gave me the strength
to avenge my family.

366
01:02:04,300 --> 01:02:07,100
Since then,
I've never looked back.

367
01:02:13,600 --> 01:02:16,000
I saw your pictures.

368
01:02:17,100 --> 01:02:19,200
Who is the woman? Your wife?

369
01:02:27,600 --> 01:02:32,300
It may be wise to keep a closer eye
on our cousins.

370
01:02:33,100 --> 01:02:36,500
I'll have raze see to it immediately.

371
01:02:36,600 --> 01:02:41,000
I'm afraid that I'm going to have
to place my faith in you, my friend.

372
01:02:41,100 --> 01:02:44,500
Time is running short.

373
01:02:45,100 --> 01:02:48,500
I tried to swerve,
but he hit us anyway.

374
01:02:50,600 --> 01:02:53,300
He sent us right into
the oncoming lane.

375
01:02:57,100 --> 01:02:59,200
When I came to...

376
01:03:00,300 --> 01:03:04,200
...i realized that part of the engine
was in the front seat.

377
01:03:04,800 --> 01:03:10,600
And she was pinned there,
6 inches from me...

378
01:03:12,800 --> 01:03:15,500
...in this horrible position.

379
01:03:19,300 --> 01:03:21,600
I think she was in shock
because she just...

380
01:03:21,800 --> 01:03:25,100
...kept asking me over
and over again if I was all right.

381
01:03:27,800 --> 01:03:29,600
She was more worried about me.

382
01:03:33,800 --> 01:03:37,800
You know, if I knew then what
I know now, I could have saved her.

383
01:03:39,300 --> 01:03:42,000
There's no doubt in my mind
about that.

384
01:03:43,800 --> 01:03:46,200
But instead she died right there...

385
01:03:47,300 --> 01:03:50,500
...about two minutes before
the ambulance arrived.

386
01:03:55,300 --> 01:03:58,900
After that, I didn't see any reason
to stick around.

387
01:03:59,300 --> 01:04:04,300
I spent a summer here with my
grandfather when I was a kid so...

388
01:04:04,300 --> 01:04:07,200
after I got my degree, I just...

389
01:04:07,800 --> 01:04:09,600
i took off.

390
01:04:12,300 --> 01:04:17,300
I came over here to move on,
to forget.

391
01:04:20,300 --> 01:04:23,200
It seemed like a good idea
at the time.

392
01:04:25,300 --> 01:04:27,300
And have you?

393
01:04:28,800 --> 01:04:30,100
Moved on?

394
01:04:31,900 --> 01:04:33,600
Have you?

395
01:04:43,100 --> 01:04:47,300
I need you to keep what I'm about to
tell you under the strictest confidence.

396
01:04:47,600 --> 01:04:49,600
It can wait.

397
01:05:15,600 --> 01:05:17,100
Who started the war?

398
01:05:17,100 --> 01:05:18,600
They did.

399
01:05:19,100 --> 01:05:22,700
Or at least that's what
we've been led to believe.

400
01:05:22,700 --> 01:05:25,800
Digging into the past is forbidden.

401
01:05:27,700 --> 01:05:29,800
I should be heading back.

402
01:05:29,800 --> 01:05:31,700
What about me?

403
01:05:32,200 --> 01:05:34,600
Viktor will know what to do.
I'll come back.

404
01:05:34,700 --> 01:05:37,400
- I won't stay alone.
- You will if you want to live.

405
01:05:37,400 --> 01:05:38,400
I want to go with you.

406
01:05:56,900 --> 01:05:58,800
What are you doing?

407
01:06:02,500 --> 01:06:04,500
When the full moon
rises tomorrow...

408
01:06:04,500 --> 01:06:08,400
...you will change, you will kill,
and you will feed.

409
01:06:08,500 --> 01:06:10,400
It's unavoidable.

410
01:06:10,500 --> 01:06:13,600
I can't leave you free
to roam around. I'm sorry.

411
01:06:19,700 --> 01:06:23,000
A single round won't kill you, but
silver prevents transformation.

412
01:06:23,200 --> 01:06:25,300
At least for a few hours.

413
01:06:25,700 --> 01:06:28,800
If I don't return in time,
do yourself a favor.

414
01:06:29,300 --> 01:06:31,200
Use it.

415
01:07:52,700 --> 01:07:53,900
Yeah?

416
01:07:54,200 --> 01:07:57,900
My lord. She's here.

417
01:08:12,200 --> 01:08:16,000
How could you do this to me?
Embarrass me like this?

418
01:08:16,200 --> 01:08:18,900
The entire coven knows
that I had plans for us.

419
01:08:19,200 --> 01:08:23,100
- There is no us!
- You'll go before Viktor...

420
01:08:23,200 --> 01:08:28,800
...and tell him exactly what I tell you to!
From here on out, you'll do as I say.

421
01:08:29,200 --> 01:08:31,600
Is that in any way unclear?

422
01:09:17,600 --> 01:09:20,400
Come closer, my child.

423
01:09:22,600 --> 01:09:24,100
Outside.

424
01:09:25,100 --> 01:09:27,000
Come on, move it.

425
01:09:36,500 --> 01:09:39,000
I've been lost without you, my lord.

426
01:09:39,000 --> 01:09:42,700
Constantly hounded by Kraven
and his never-ending infatuation.

427
01:09:45,500 --> 01:09:49,200
It is the oldest story in the book.

428
01:09:49,500 --> 01:09:54,500
He desires the one thing
he cannot have.

429
01:09:56,300 --> 01:09:59,400
Now, tell me...

430
01:10:00,300 --> 01:10:03,700
...why have you come to believe
that Lucian still lives?

431
01:10:05,900 --> 01:10:08,600
- Yeah.
- I've given you all the proof you need.

432
01:10:08,900 --> 01:10:13,800
Incoherent thoughts and images,
nothing more.

433
01:10:13,900 --> 01:10:17,300
Which is precisely why the awakening
is performed by an elder.

434
01:10:17,900 --> 01:10:20,200
You do not possess
the necessary skills.

435
01:10:20,400 --> 01:10:23,200
But I did see Lucian. I shot him.
You must believe me.

436
01:10:23,400 --> 01:10:26,600
The chain has never been broken.
Not once.

437
01:10:26,600 --> 01:10:28,600
Not in 14 centuries.

438
01:10:28,900 --> 01:10:33,000
Not since we elders first began
to leapfrog through time.

439
01:10:33,400 --> 01:10:36,400
One awake, two asleep.
That's the way of it.

440
01:10:36,400 --> 01:10:39,600
It is Marcus' turn to reign,
not mine.

441
01:10:39,900 --> 01:10:42,700
- There's been a complication.
- But I had no choice.

442
01:10:42,900 --> 01:10:45,900
The coven is in danger,
and Michael is the key...

443
01:10:48,900 --> 01:10:50,800
yes.

444
01:10:50,900 --> 01:10:53,100
The lycan.

445
01:10:55,400 --> 01:10:57,400
Please.

446
01:10:57,900 --> 01:11:00,200
Give me the chance
to get proof you require.

447
01:11:00,400 --> 01:11:01,400
Fine.

448
01:11:01,400 --> 01:11:05,400
I will leave it to Kraven
to collect the proof...

449
01:11:05,900 --> 01:11:08,500
...if there is any.

450
01:11:09,900 --> 01:11:11,900
How could you trust him over me?

451
01:11:12,400 --> 01:11:17,500
Because he is not the one who
has been tainted by an animal.

452
01:11:19,400 --> 01:11:21,800
I love you...

453
01:11:24,400 --> 01:11:28,700
...like a daughter,
but you leave me with no choice.

454
01:11:28,900 --> 01:11:31,900
These rules are in place
for a good reason...

455
01:11:31,900 --> 01:11:37,200
...and they are the only reason
we have survived this long.

456
01:11:41,400 --> 01:11:45,400
You will not be shown
an ounce of leniency.

457
01:11:46,000 --> 01:11:51,400
When Amelia arrives, the council
will convene and decide your fate.

458
01:11:52,000 --> 01:11:55,100
You have broken the chain
and the covenant!

459
01:11:55,500 --> 01:11:57,900
You must be judged!

460
01:12:22,000 --> 01:12:25,200
You should've listened to me
and stayed out of this.

461
01:12:25,500 --> 01:12:30,000
Now you'll be lucky if I can convince
the council to spare your life.

462
01:12:30,100 --> 01:12:31,700
Tell me.

463
01:12:32,000 --> 01:12:36,500
Did you have the nerve to cut the skin
from his arm, or did Lucian do it?

464
01:12:42,500 --> 01:12:44,700
Mark my words.

465
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:47,900
Soon, you'll be
seeing things my way.

466
01:12:58,000 --> 01:13:01,500
No one opens this door.
Understood?

467
01:13:03,000 --> 01:13:07,100
I can't afford to have my future queen
run off with that lycan again.

468
01:13:45,900 --> 01:13:47,600
Shit.

469
01:13:57,400 --> 01:14:01,400
Change of plans. Amelia will be
picked up by Soren and his team.

470
01:14:01,800 --> 01:14:05,700
- That's our job.
- Not anymore.

471
01:16:57,300 --> 01:17:01,300
- Why are you helping me?
- I'm not. I'm helping me.

472
01:17:40,500 --> 01:17:43,900
- What's going on?
- The perimeter sensor's been tripped.

473
01:17:44,000 --> 01:17:46,400
We're locking down the mansion.

474
01:17:47,000 --> 01:17:50,000
It's Selene. She's escaped,
to go to him, to Michael.

475
01:17:50,500 --> 01:17:55,300
I want that lycan's head on a plate.

476
01:19:26,600 --> 01:19:28,400
We need to go.

477
01:19:57,200 --> 01:19:58,200
Get down!

478
01:20:01,200 --> 01:20:03,900
Go. Go.

479
01:20:10,100 --> 01:20:12,400
- Jump.
- Are you fucking kidding me?

480
01:21:35,100 --> 01:21:38,100
- Any luck?
- False alarm.

481
01:21:38,100 --> 01:21:42,500
The dogs would've been all over it
if anything had gotten near that fence.

482
01:21:43,100 --> 01:21:46,400
- Amelia should have arrived by now.
- Yes.

483
01:21:50,600 --> 01:21:54,900
Look, I want you to slip off the property
and find out what's keeping her.

484
01:21:55,100 --> 01:21:56,900
You've got it.

485
01:22:35,200 --> 01:22:37,700
Maybe we should pull over
and dose him.

486
01:22:37,700 --> 01:22:40,700
Fuck him. He'll be all right.
We're almost there.

487
01:23:46,500 --> 01:23:50,400
Oh, shit. He's not gonna make it.
Pull over. Pull over!

488
01:24:09,100 --> 01:24:10,700
Get the kit.

489
01:24:24,000 --> 01:24:26,100
Stick him. Stick him.

490
01:24:37,400 --> 01:24:39,100
My lord.

491
01:24:40,400 --> 01:24:43,100
Viktor wants to speak with you.

492
01:25:08,800 --> 01:25:10,600
My lord.

493
01:25:14,800 --> 01:25:17,400
I sent for Selene...

494
01:25:17,800 --> 01:25:19,800
...not you.

495
01:25:20,300 --> 01:25:22,900
She's defied your orders...

496
01:25:24,800 --> 01:25:26,700
...and fled the mansion, my lord.

497
01:25:27,300 --> 01:25:31,300
Your incompetence
is becoming most taxing.

498
01:25:31,300 --> 01:25:35,200
It's not my fault.
She's become obsessed...

499
01:25:35,300 --> 01:25:38,700
...thinks that I'm at the core
of some ridiculous conspiracy.

500
01:25:39,300 --> 01:25:41,300
And here's my proof.

501
01:25:55,300 --> 01:25:58,500
Now, I want you to tell them
exactly what you told me.

502
01:26:06,100 --> 01:26:09,300
All right, all right.

503
01:26:11,100 --> 01:26:16,300
We've been searching for someone
with a special trait.

504
01:26:16,300 --> 01:26:20,400
A direct descendant
of Alexander Corvinus...

505
01:26:20,600 --> 01:26:24,200
...hungarian, a warlord...

506
01:26:24,600 --> 01:26:29,200
...who came to power in the early
seasons of the fifth century.

507
01:26:29,200 --> 01:26:35,600
Just in time to watch a plague
ravage his village.

508
01:26:36,600 --> 01:26:39,800
He alone survived.

509
01:26:41,100 --> 01:26:46,000
Somehow, his body
was able to change the disease...

510
01:26:46,100 --> 01:26:50,000
...mold it to his benefit.

511
01:26:50,100 --> 01:26:55,300
He became the first true immortal.

512
01:27:03,700 --> 01:27:07,500
And years later,
he fathered at least two children...

513
01:27:07,700 --> 01:27:10,000
...who inherited this same trait.

514
01:27:10,200 --> 01:27:13,400
The sons of the Corvinus clan.

515
01:27:13,700 --> 01:27:16,900
One bitten by bat, one by wolf...

516
01:27:17,200 --> 01:27:22,500
...one to walk the lonely road
of mortality as a human.

517
01:27:22,700 --> 01:27:28,100
- It's a ridiculous legend. Nothing!
- That may be...

518
01:27:30,200 --> 01:27:33,500
...but our species
do have a common ancestor.

519
01:27:34,200 --> 01:27:37,800
A mutation of the original virus...

520
01:27:38,200 --> 01:27:40,400
...is directly linked to his bloodline.

521
01:27:40,700 --> 01:27:45,500
There is a descendant
of Corvinus lying there...

522
01:27:46,600 --> 01:27:48,700
...not three feet from you.

523
01:27:48,700 --> 01:27:50,300
Yes.

524
01:27:51,100 --> 01:27:56,200
But he's already a vampire.
We needed a pure source...

525
01:27:57,100 --> 01:28:02,300
...untainted. An exact duplicate
of the original virus...

526
01:28:02,600 --> 01:28:04,600
<i>...which we learned...</i>

527
01:28:05,100 --> 01:28:09,500
<i>...was hidden away in the genetic
code of his human descendants...</i>

528
01:28:09,600 --> 01:28:14,700
<i>...and passed along
in its latent form...</i>

529
01:28:15,600 --> 01:28:18,500
<i>...down through the ages...</i>

530
01:28:18,600 --> 01:28:23,500
<i>...all the way to Michael Corvin.</i>

531
01:28:24,600 --> 01:28:29,600
For years, we tried to combine
their bloodlines.

532
01:28:33,200 --> 01:28:36,300
<i>And for years we failed.</i>

533
01:28:36,700 --> 01:28:38,800
<i>It was useless.</i>

534
01:28:40,200 --> 01:28:44,800
Even at the cellular level, our species
seemed destined to destroy each other.

535
01:28:47,700 --> 01:28:52,600
That is, until we found Michael.

536
01:28:55,700 --> 01:29:00,700
<i>The Corvinus strain allows
for a perfect union.</i>

537
01:29:03,200 --> 01:29:06,500
A triple-celled platelet...

538
01:29:07,700 --> 01:29:12,600
...which holds unspeakable power.

539
01:29:12,700 --> 01:29:15,900
There can be no such union.

540
01:29:16,700 --> 01:29:21,300
- And to speak of it is heresy.
- We'll see.

541
01:29:22,700 --> 01:29:27,200
Once Lucian has injected himself
with Michael's blood.

542
01:29:27,700 --> 01:29:30,200
Lucian is dead.

543
01:29:30,300 --> 01:29:32,700
According to whom?

544
01:29:43,200 --> 01:29:45,200
I need you to do something for me.

545
01:29:52,200 --> 01:29:55,100
I can assure you, my child...

546
01:29:55,700 --> 01:29:58,000
...Kraven will pay with his life.

547
01:30:18,700 --> 01:30:23,000
Soon, this house will lie in ruins.

548
01:30:23,200 --> 01:30:25,600
- Not before you.
- No, wait. Wait.

549
01:30:26,200 --> 01:30:29,200
You and you alone
will know the truth of this.

550
01:30:32,700 --> 01:30:38,300
If Lucian was able to get his hands
on the blood of a pure-born...

551
01:30:38,700 --> 01:30:43,800
...a powerful elder like Amelia...

552
01:30:43,800 --> 01:30:47,400
...or yourself...

553
01:30:47,700 --> 01:30:52,300
...and inject it along
with Michael's blood...

554
01:30:52,700 --> 01:30:54,800
abomination.

555
01:30:54,800 --> 01:30:56,900
Half-vampire...

556
01:30:57,200 --> 01:31:01,500
...half-lycan, but stronger than both.

557
01:31:20,700 --> 01:31:22,100
I need to speak with Kahn.

558
01:31:29,800 --> 01:31:31,400
My lord...

559
01:31:32,600 --> 01:31:36,000
...the council members
have been assassinated.

560
01:31:39,600 --> 01:31:42,900
- What of Amelia?
- They bled her dry.

561
01:31:45,400 --> 01:31:49,000
It has already begun.

562
01:32:00,400 --> 01:32:02,900
I'm sorry I doubted you.

563
01:32:03,500 --> 01:32:08,700
Fear not, my child,
absolution will be yours...

564
01:32:10,500 --> 01:32:15,500
...the moment you kill the descendant
of Corvinus, this...

565
01:32:16,500 --> 01:32:18,700
...Michael.

566
01:32:54,000 --> 01:32:58,300
You've been given an enzyme
to stop the change.

567
01:32:58,500 --> 01:33:04,000
It may take a little time
for the grogginess to dissipate.

568
01:33:10,400 --> 01:33:12,200
That's enough!

569
01:33:12,400 --> 01:33:16,900
Just go and see
what's keeping raze, will you?

570
01:33:18,800 --> 01:33:20,500
I really must apologize.

571
01:33:21,300 --> 01:33:24,200
He's in desperate need
of a lesson in manners.

572
01:33:24,300 --> 01:33:27,700
Speaking of manners,
where are mine? Forgive me.

573
01:33:28,300 --> 01:33:30,300
I'm Lucian.

574
01:33:32,300 --> 01:33:34,600
I need to go.

575
01:33:35,800 --> 01:33:37,300
I need to get back.

576
01:33:39,200 --> 01:33:41,600
There's no going back.

577
01:33:42,200 --> 01:33:44,700
There's no going anywhere.

578
01:33:45,200 --> 01:33:50,100
The vampires will kill you on sight.
Just for being what you are.

579
01:33:50,200 --> 01:33:52,000
One of us.

580
01:33:55,200 --> 01:33:58,100
You are one of us.

581
01:34:01,200 --> 01:34:02,500
What are you doing?

582
01:34:03,200 --> 01:34:06,800
- What are you doing?
- Bringing an end to this conflict.

583
01:34:13,600 --> 01:34:16,300
Your war, it has nothing
to do with me.

584
01:34:16,700 --> 01:34:18,700
My war?

585
01:34:41,400 --> 01:34:43,600
No!

586
01:34:44,100 --> 01:34:45,500
No!

587
01:34:46,500 --> 01:34:49,000
No!

588
01:35:20,100 --> 01:35:22,500
No!

589
01:35:25,200 --> 01:35:27,000
No! No!

590
01:35:36,500 --> 01:35:40,300
Sonja!

591
01:36:44,000 --> 01:36:47,100
They forced you to watch her die.

592
01:36:49,300 --> 01:36:51,200
Sonja.

593
01:36:52,800 --> 01:36:55,500
That's what started the war.

594
01:36:58,800 --> 01:37:02,100
I saw it happen as if I were there.

595
01:37:06,800 --> 01:37:09,400
We were slaves once.

596
01:37:10,800 --> 01:37:14,600
The daylight guardians
of the vampires.

597
01:37:16,300 --> 01:37:19,000
I was born in servitude...

598
01:37:20,900 --> 01:37:23,700
...yet I harbored them no ill will.

599
01:37:24,900 --> 01:37:27,800
I even took a vampire for my bride.

600
01:37:28,900 --> 01:37:30,800
It was forbidden...

601
01:37:30,900 --> 01:37:33,100
...our union.

602
01:37:33,400 --> 01:37:38,300
Viktor feared
a blending of the species.

603
01:37:39,900 --> 01:37:42,200
Feared it so much...

604
01:37:43,400 --> 01:37:45,400
...he killed her.

605
01:37:46,400 --> 01:37:48,500
His own daughter...

606
01:37:49,900 --> 01:37:52,100
...burnt alive...

607
01:37:54,900 --> 01:37:56,900
...for loving me.

608
01:37:59,900 --> 01:38:02,200
This is his war...

609
01:38:02,200 --> 01:38:04,500
...Viktor's...

610
01:38:05,900 --> 01:38:09,100
...and he's spent the last 600 years...

611
01:38:09,900 --> 01:38:13,100
...exterminating my species.

612
01:38:14,400 --> 01:38:17,100
What are they gonna do to Selene?

613
01:38:19,900 --> 01:38:21,300
We have company.

614
01:38:22,900 --> 01:38:26,700
- I thought we had a deal.
- Patience.

615
01:38:28,900 --> 01:38:30,400
Kraven.

616
01:38:30,400 --> 01:38:33,700
These are matters
to be discussed in private.

617
01:38:34,900 --> 01:38:39,600
Please escort our guests downstairs.

618
01:38:55,400 --> 01:38:58,400
The council has been destroyed.

619
01:38:59,400 --> 01:39:02,300
Soon, you will have it all.

620
01:39:02,400 --> 01:39:08,400
Both great covens and an ironclad
peace treaty with the lycans.

621
01:39:08,400 --> 01:39:12,800
Who I trust will not be forgotten
when the spoils are tabulated.

622
01:39:12,900 --> 01:39:17,000
How do you expect me to assume
control now that Viktor's awake?

623
01:39:17,400 --> 01:39:21,000
There's no defeating him.
He grows stronger as we speak.

624
01:39:21,000 --> 01:39:25,100
And that is precisely why
I need Michael.

625
01:39:25,400 --> 01:39:27,800
If Viktor were so easy to dispatch...

626
01:39:28,400 --> 01:39:31,500
...you'd have done it yourself
centuries ago.

627
01:39:42,500 --> 01:39:44,700
Exit shaft! Move it!

628
01:39:47,500 --> 01:39:49,300
Son of a bitch!

629
01:40:04,000 --> 01:40:06,100
Oh, shit!

630
01:40:18,700 --> 01:40:20,400
It's Viktor.

631
01:40:20,700 --> 01:40:22,400
Yes.

632
01:40:22,700 --> 01:40:26,000
And if you had done your job,
he'd still be in hibernation.

633
01:40:32,300 --> 01:40:34,200
Where the hell is raze?

634
01:40:37,300 --> 01:40:39,400
Is there another way out?

635
01:40:40,300 --> 01:40:45,700
I guess it didn't occur to you that you'll
have to bleed to pull off this coup.

636
01:40:49,200 --> 01:40:51,800
Don't even think about leaving.

637
01:41:13,200 --> 01:41:17,200
Silver nitrate.
Bet you weren't expecting that.

638
01:41:26,700 --> 01:41:29,700
Come on! Move! Move! Move!
Move! Move!

639
01:42:52,200 --> 01:42:53,900
Lucian.

640
01:44:49,600 --> 01:44:51,400
Selene!

641
01:44:52,600 --> 01:44:54,300
Selene!

642
01:45:40,700 --> 01:45:42,500
Not yet.

643
01:50:32,500 --> 01:50:35,000
I have to get you out.
Viktor's on his way.

644
01:50:35,000 --> 01:50:38,000
And he won't be satisfied
until every lycan's dead.

645
01:50:39,000 --> 01:50:41,600
They'll kill you too,
just for helping me.

646
01:50:42,000 --> 01:50:43,400
I know.

647
01:51:06,400 --> 01:51:08,800
I know what started the war.

648
01:53:19,100 --> 01:53:21,000
That's enough.
You're coming with me!

649
01:53:22,100 --> 01:53:24,600
I hope I live to see
Viktor choke the life from you!

650
01:53:24,700 --> 01:53:26,600
I bet you do.

651
01:53:27,100 --> 01:53:30,800
But let me tell you a little something
about your beloved dark father.

652
01:53:32,100 --> 01:53:34,600
He's the one who killed your family.

653
01:53:35,000 --> 01:53:36,900
Not the lycans.

654
01:53:37,500 --> 01:53:39,500
Never could follow his own rules.

655
01:53:39,500 --> 01:53:41,900
Said he couldn't abide the taste
of livestock.

656
01:53:42,000 --> 01:53:46,300
So every once in a while, he went out
and gorged himself on human blood.

657
01:53:47,100 --> 01:53:49,000
I kept his secrets...

658
01:53:49,600 --> 01:53:51,100
...cleaned up the mess.

659
01:53:51,600 --> 01:53:53,500
But it was he...

660
01:53:53,600 --> 01:53:55,200
...who crept room to room...

661
01:53:55,600 --> 01:53:58,900
...dispatching everyone
close to your heart.

662
01:53:59,600 --> 01:54:01,700
But when he got to you...

663
01:54:02,100 --> 01:54:06,000
...he just couldn't bear the thought
of draining you dry.

664
01:54:06,100 --> 01:54:11,100
You, who reminded him so much
of his precious sonja...

665
01:54:12,100 --> 01:54:16,100
...the daughter
he condemned to death.

666
01:54:16,600 --> 01:54:19,700
- Lies.
- Believe what you want.

667
01:54:20,600 --> 01:54:22,300
Now come on.

668
01:54:22,600 --> 01:54:24,900
Your place is by my side.

669
01:54:32,000 --> 01:54:33,900
So be it.

670
01:55:03,000 --> 01:55:04,300
Bite him!

671
01:55:08,100 --> 01:55:10,000
<i>Half-vampire...</i>

672
01:55:10,100 --> 01:55:11,800
<i>...half-lycan...</i>

673
01:55:12,100 --> 01:55:14,900
<i>...but stronger than both.</i>

674
01:55:40,900 --> 01:55:43,400
What the hell are you doing?

675
01:55:43,900 --> 01:55:46,400
You may have killed me...

676
01:55:47,400 --> 01:55:48,900
...cousin.

677
01:55:49,000 --> 01:55:50,400
But my will...

678
01:55:50,700 --> 01:55:53,300
...is done regardless.

679
01:56:33,400 --> 01:56:35,300
Where is he?

680
01:56:36,400 --> 01:56:37,700
Where's Kraven?

681
01:56:59,200 --> 01:57:01,600
Forgive me, my child.

682
01:57:02,700 --> 01:57:04,600
It wasn't the lycans.

683
01:57:06,700 --> 01:57:08,500
It was you.

684
01:57:15,700 --> 01:57:17,600
Leave us.

685
01:57:36,200 --> 01:57:38,600
How could you bear my trust...

686
01:57:38,700 --> 01:57:41,100
...knowing that you'd
killed my family?

687
01:57:42,700 --> 01:57:44,400
Yes.

688
01:57:44,700 --> 01:57:46,600
I have taken from you.

689
01:57:48,200 --> 01:57:51,300
But I have given so much more.

690
01:57:52,200 --> 01:57:57,400
Is it not a fair trade, the life I have
granted you? The gift of immortality?

691
01:57:57,800 --> 01:58:00,400
And the life of your daughter?

692
01:58:00,800 --> 01:58:03,200
Your own flesh and blood?

693
01:58:24,100 --> 01:58:26,800
I loved my daughter!

694
01:58:29,100 --> 01:58:31,500
But the abomination growing
in her womb...

695
01:58:31,600 --> 01:58:34,300
...was a betrayal of me
and of the coven!

696
01:58:39,600 --> 01:58:43,500
I did what was necessary
to protect the species...

697
01:58:43,600 --> 01:58:47,100
...as I am forced to do yet again.

698
01:58:50,900 --> 01:58:53,000
No!

699
02:01:45,600 --> 02:01:47,200
Time to die.

700
02:05:07,200 --> 02:05:09,900
<i>Though I cannot predict the future...</i>

701
02:05:10,200 --> 02:05:13,800
<i>...the consequences of tonight
will reverberate through the halls...</i>

702
02:05:13,800 --> 02:05:16,900
<i>...of both great covens
for many years to come.</i>

703
02:05:18,200 --> 02:05:21,000
<i>Two vampire elders
have been slain...</i>

704
02:05:21,200 --> 02:05:23,500
<i>...one by my own hand.</i>

705
02:05:25,300 --> 02:05:29,100
<i>Soon, Marcus will take the throne.</i>

706
02:05:30,300 --> 02:05:34,900
<i>And a tide of anger and retribution
will spill out into the night.</i>

707
02:05:36,800 --> 02:05:39,400
<i>Differences will be set aside.</i>

708
02:05:40,300 --> 02:05:42,600
<i>Allegiances will be made.</i>

709
02:05:42,800 --> 02:05:44,300
<i>And soon...</i>

710
02:05:44,800 --> 02:05:47,400
<i>...I will become the hunted.</i>
